<p>Shnatz (שנ״צ) in Hebrew (the tz as the zz in pizza) is an abbreviation of two Hebrew words, <a href="https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%A9%D7%A0%D7%AA_%D7%A6%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%99%D7%9D">שנת צהריים</a>, which means noon sleep. In the US, this is known as <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siesta">Siesta</a>, borrowed from Spanish, because the concept of a noon nap is as alien to Americans as a baconless breakfast, so we don&rsquo;t have a word for it here.</p>
